<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 32,352 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 32,352 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 32,352 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday, compared to 54,181 tonnes in the same period on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Thursday    December 11</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 5,165	13,000</p>
<p>    Import cargo		27,187	41,181</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and seven berthed. In the next 24 hours, four are expected to sail and 13 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     31,499	 Sylva		  13/12</p>
<p>Tallow		    3,840	 Vanine		 14/12</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Al-Maqwa	     14/12</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     25,500	 Sava		   15/12</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
